    899  f115							; --- Player sprite: color for THIS line, graphics byte for NEXT line ---
    900  f115							; GRP0 written on line S displays on line S+1 (latched at the sprite's
    901  f115							; window start after the write) — index graphics with A0+1 ($ff wraps
    902  f115							; to 0 = row0 on the line before the sprite).
    903  f115							; CORRECTED 2026-10-22 (Phase 4): that "line S+1" is only true for a
    904  f115							; sprite whose pixels come AFTER the store. Per Stella's Player::grp /
    905  f115							; updatePattern, a GRP write lands in myPatternNew and renders at once, so
    906  f115							; the boundary is the sprite's own pixel start (cycle ~(61+X)/3). With
    907  f115							; VDELP0=1 (set in the VBL, see the comment there) the live pattern is
    908  f115							; `myPatternOld`, latched by the GRP1 store at c58, so P0 is correct for
    909  f115							; every X < 113 px and its art row r sits on the SAME scanline as
    910  f115							; PlayerColTable[r] (COLUP0 lands at c19, before all pixels) — i.e. the
    911  f115							; art and its per-row colours finally agree. Do not reorder the colour
    912  f115							; path behind the graphics: COLUP0 must stay the first store in the body.
    913  f115							; Running-Y: Y = A0 = Scanline - RoomY is computed ONCE at kernel entry
    914  f115							; (sec/sbc RoomY/tay); .Line's iny advances it (Y = A0+1 after the
    915  f115							; graphics write = A0 of the next line). Nothing between rows may touch
    916  f115							; Y — the water-strip band-color read is an inlined `lda` (Y untouched).
    917  f115							; Cycle budget — MEASURED (sim_frame_budget, bugs.md #29 Class A):
    918  f115							; the old worst path (in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range) was
    919  f115							; 78c: WSYNC write landed 2c into the next line -> full-line stall ->
    920  f115							; +1 scanline on every frame whose object window overlapped the A0=11
    921  f115							; line (24 stalls in the SIM_LEVEL=2 window, always even frames —
    922  f115							; SelectActiveObject parity rotation). Root fix: the color/beam gate
    923  f115							; below stops at A0=10; row 11 inherits row 10's COLUP0/ENAM0 writes
    924  f115							; (PlayerColTable [10]==[11], verify_build asserts) because
    925  f115							; GRP0 row11 is fetched on line A0=10 already ("row11 shows via
    926  f115							; line10"). Worst path measured 2026-10-15 (vcrunch jitter hunt):
    927  f115							; in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range = 69c between WSs,
    928  f115							; start-to-start d=72 — was 73/76 (= stall zone 74-76, whole-screen
    929  f115							; +1-line jitter) until the dead `cpy #12 / bcs .GrpZero` (4c, never
    930  f115							; taken on the A0<=10 color path) moved to .GrpSkip. Budget: work
    931  f115							; <= 70c / d <= 73 — a 74-76 segment stalls a full scanline.
    932  f115							; ObjSprites+107 must stay in ONE page (else lda ObjSprites,X
    933  f115							; page-crosses, +1c on the GRP1 fetch) — verify_build enforces this.
    934  f115							; Branch targets all same-page (3c taken) and PlayerColTable in $F8xx
    935  f115							; (verify_build guards the A0=10 page-cross budget).
    936  f115							; GRP1 object section clobbers X (ObjSprites index) — row counter lives in
    937  f115							; RowIdx and X is reloaded after bne. Row-advance +6c on the .Row setup
    938  f115							; scanline (segment 63c -> 69c <= 76c): frame length unchanged.
    939  f115							; The old Scanline/sec/sbc/tay prefix cost 10c more (body 66c -> WSYNC
    940  f115							; write on cycle 76 = one cycle late): WSYNC stalled a full line per
    941  f115							; overlapping scanline — stretched cave row, HUD pushed down, and with
    942  f115							; GRP1 flicker rotation the frame length alternated (one-tile oscillation).
    943  f115							; Keep the hot path at <= 70c work: an overrun duplicates the scanline.
    944  f115		       c0 15		      cpy	#PLAYER_SPRITE_H - 1
    945  f117		       b0 3d		      bcs	.GrpSkip	; A0 >= 11 (incl $ff): no color/beam this line.
