   3845  fe0c							; ==============================================================================
   3846  fe0c							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   3847  fe0c							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   3848  fe0c							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   3849  fe0c							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   3850  fe0c							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   3851  fe0c							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   3852  fe0c							;
   3853  fe0c							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   3854  fe0c							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   3855  fe0c							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   3856  fe0c							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   3857  fe0c							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   3858  fe0c							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   3859  fe0c							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
   3860  fe0c							;
   3861  fe0c							; StageSlot1 (VBLANK, after SelectActiveObject): stages ObjBase1/ObjTop1/ObjX1,
   3862  fe0c							; $FF = none. Slot 1 = the miner or the first live enemy whose Y is in a band
   3863  fe0c							; above slot 0's. The KEY skip mirrors the slot-0 path (KeyHeld = LevelStartRoom
   3864  fe0c							; b7). Tally frames ($FE) are gated out: EnemyRamY holds score-pointer bytes
   3865  fe0c							; then (AGENTS: tally frame draws the MINER only).
